From 36e76e1f2072a538a9927cecf9c495290d97402a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:02:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(unloaded): gate notices on orphan subs and
 remote_notices on settled ledger (host_pass idle CPU)

Hub profile (600 s idle, py-spy): notices held hot by ONE orphan sub (chat in no store, task done 6 d),
remote_notices hot because any terminal card was 'hot' and the key held the replica commit counter.
notices: an orphan sub (chat in no profile store, card not archived, no inflight claim) is part of the key, not a reason to run.
remote_notices: hot only while an owed notice lacks a settled ledger row, a holder-claimed row exists, a chat is open or a wake runs; key is the card digest + ledger revision.
